      "refersTo": "selected-area",
      "description": "Desktop overlay with score and evidence disclosure. Preview values are illustrative, not observations.",
      "html": "<article class=\"ds-detail\"><h2>Southampton</h2><div class=\"ds-detail-score\">50.0 <span>/ 100 intensity</span></div><p>Experimental estimate · no observed pedestrian counts</p><details><summary>Raw estimate &amp; sensitivity</summary></details></article>",
      "css": ".ds-detail{display:flex;flex-direction:column;width:330px;padding:16px;background:var(--surface,#ffffff);color:var(--ink,#203e30);border-radius:14px;box-shadow:var(--shadow,0 8px 30px #183c2420);font-family:\"Segoe UI\",system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-detail h2{margin:12px 0 0;font-size:23px;font-weight:650;letter-spacing:-.03em;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.ds-detail-score{padding:18px 0;font-size:34px;font-weight:650;line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.035em;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-detail-score span{font-size:11px;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:0;color:var(--muted,#536655)}.ds-detail p{font-size:10px;color:var(--muted,#536655);margin:9px 0 16px}.ds-detail summary{font-size:12px;font-weight:550;padding:13px 1px;border-top:1px solid var(--line,#dce4d8);cursor:pointer}.ds-detail summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #709345;outline-offset:3px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Activity intensity legend",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "intensity-legend",
      "description": "Shared continuous scale with separate unknown and modelled-low/zero keys.",
      "html": "<aside class=\"ds-legend\" aria-label=\"Activity intensity\"><strong>Activity intensity</strong><div class=\"ds-gradient\"></div><div class=\"ds-ticks\"><span>0 · Low</span><span>50</span><span>100 · High</span></div><p>Fixed scale · not people or a percentile.</p><p class=\"ds-key\"><i class=\"ds-gap\"></i>Grey dashes: coverage unknown</p><p class=\"ds-key\"><i class=\"ds-zero\"></i>Pale: modelled low / zero</p><p>Assumed patterns · no live observations</p></aside>",
      "css": ".ds-legend{width:252px;padding:14px;border-radius:12px;background:var(--surface,#ffffff);color:var(--ink,#203e30);box-shadow:var(--shadow,0 8px 30px #183c2420);font-family:\"Segoe UI\",system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-legend strong{font-size:12px;font-weight:600}.ds-gradient{height:9px;border-radius:3px;margin:8px 0 5px;border:1px solid var(--line,#dce4d8);background:linear-gradient(to right,#edf3ea 0%,#c6d8b8 25%,#88ad78 50%,#457a53 75%,#12482f 100%)}.ds-ticks{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:10px;color:var(--muted,#536655)}.ds-legend p{font-size:10px;line-height:1.5;margin:6px 0 0;color:var(--muted,#536655)}.ds-key{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px}.ds-key i{display:inline-block;width:16px;height:10px}.ds-gap{background:#98a59c22;border:1px dashed #71857b}.ds-zero{background:#edf3ea;border:1px solid #b5c9ac}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){.ds-gradient{border-color:#849779}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Fieldnotes",
    "overview": "Fieldnotes is a functional map workspace with a restrained dark green identity,\npale paper surfaces and compact supporting controls. The map carries spatial\ninformation; the explorer supplies time, filters and ranked areas; selected-area\ndetails make the estimate inspectable. Dark mode preserves this hierarchy with\nforest surfaces and light sage text.\n\nThis records the implemented V2 interface, using PROJECT.md as product authority.\nThe CSS and React components are the implementation evidence; this file and its\nsidecar describe their reusable visual rules. Typography remains the incumbent\nsystem sans. The interface keeps experimental status, missing coverage and model\nassumptions visible alongside numerical results.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Map-first desktop and mobile composition.",
      "Restrained green identity with tonal paper surfaces.",
      "Compact controls and tabular numerical comparisons.",
      "Progressive evidence disclosures and explicit missingness.",
      "Functional, input-aware motion."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "Missingness",
        "body": "Coverage unknown must remain visually and verbally distinct from modelled zero; neither state establishes actual emptiness.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "Number",
        "body": "Preserve tabular numerals for comparisons and keep intensity, city rank, relative raw units and assumption sensitivity separately labelled.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "Overlay",
        "body": "Reserve the shared soft shadow for surfaces that overlap the map; use dividers and tonal selection for ranked rows.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep the map primary and make evidence reachable through the explorer and selected-area disclosures.",
      "Do use the shared intensity ramp and fixed mapping for the map, legend and hourly intensity display.",
      "Do retain separate labels for intensity, unrounded city rank, relative raw units and assumption sensitivity.",
      "Do preserve focus outlines, labelled sheet controls, safe-area spacing and instant keyboard/reduced-motion sheet changes.",
      "Do show coverage unknown separately from modelled zero and keep the experimental caveat visible."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't normalize intensity to the current viewport, hour, filter or current maximum.",
      "Don't present intensity as a percentile, headcount, accuracy rating, female presence or encounter probability.",
      "Don't use the whole map or sheet content as a sheet drag surface.",
      "Don't treat compact legacy metadata or undersized secondary controls as ideals for new surfaces.",
      "Don't add a new brand palette, decorative display face or blanket card shadow without a new design decision."
    ]
  }
}
